  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking lists the largest federal contracts by total value for FY2026 to date. The top entry is HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC at $51.3B. The list measures full contract values, not single-year obligations. That means the numbers reflect the total value of awarded contracts over their lifetimes rather than the portion paid in FY2026. The ranking shows a mix of healthcare, defense prime contractors, and national laboratory managers among the largest contract holders. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP appears twice under similar names with values of $48.1B and $35.1B. Multiple national laboratory management contracts appear among the top ten, including NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC at $42.6B, UT-BATTELLE LLC at $42.1B, and LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC at $41.2B. The total obligations figure shown for the period is $51.3B, which matches the largest single contract value on the list. Readers should note the page focus: total award value rather than annual spending or obligations.",
    "sections": [
